assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount > Old_arrListCount && Old_arrListContainsX && !New_arrListContainsX); 

// @@@ if arraylist.count is decreased after removing x, then arraylist.contains(x) should be true before and after remove(x) is called
assert.IsTrue(New_arrListCount < Old_arrListCount && Old_arrListContainsX && New_arrListContainsX);
```

Please note: The order of old and new states might be swapped in some assertions, but you can use weak assertions (e.g., assert.IsFalse instead of assert.IsTrue) as these assertions are based on properties and not a definitive correctness of the method.

